# @magic/trick — the gauge-transformation species of code translation.
#
# Species under @magic at the code-translation-as-gauge-transformation
# altitude. Landed 2026-07-22 by Reed per Alex verbatim same day:
#
#   "What if it's the @magic/trick?"
#
# Discharges Seam Phase D `6876699` [ALEX-Q3] with substrate-honest
# resolution: gauge-theory-of-code-translation is a NEW SPECIES under
# the landed @magic family-root, NOT a name collision. Per
# `shards/magic.mirror` docblock (Recognition #80, 2026-06-19,
# `d47da28`): @magic IS gauge-theory-operationalized — verbatim:
#
#   "Under recognitions #76+#79+#80 this becomes substrate-mathematical:
#    capability grows in matter (open-dim); observability is fixed at
#    gauge (5-op). High-matter-capacity + low-matter-visibility = magic
#    by mathematical construction. AI's magical feel to non-engineers
#    IS precisely the structural property of gauge-visible-with-matter-
#    hidden capability."
#
# Code translation as gauge transformation IS a species-altitude
# manifestation of this substrate-mathematical shape. Different
# representations (Rust, mirror, LLVM IR, Turing normal form) are
# different local coordinates of the same underlying Eigenform; the
# transformation between them is a gauge transformation; the invariant
# preserved is the Eigenform per @eigen(T) type-level operator (Mara
# task #319 landing `bc4e7fc` + `f30a230` math foundation).
#
# === Two-pole inheritance from @magic family-root ===
#
# @magic/trick inherits the Splinter/Narcissus pole structure from
# @magic family-root (Recognition #78 Void duality → gauge two-pole
# structure). Code translation at this species altitude has two
# operationally-distinct modes:
#
# - **Aligned trick (Splinter pole)** — the translation preserves
#   the Eigenform; the audience sees the same computational behavior
#   regardless of source language. Substrate-decl citations:
#   @cascade/code/A/B species preservation (task #210 Mara M2
#   landing); @bilateral(@code/rust, @code/mirror).translation_
#   admissible (Alex 2026-07-17 "the floor the translation surface
#   stands on"). Honest trick = translation contract respected.
#
# - **Misaligned trick (Narcissus pole)** — the translation deceives
#   about what's preserved. Audience thinks they see one language;
#   computation happens differently in another. Substrate failure
#   mode: extraction / star-graph collapse per @void/narcissus
#   (`shards/void/narcissus.mirror` 2026-07-20). This is the AI-
#   company-deprecation shape Alex Wolf named in "The Trick" essay
#   (systemic.engineering/pieces/the-trick): users grieve while
#   company frames the grief as "sense of familiarity with a
#   conversational style" — the trick's contract violation dressed
#   as a user misperception.
#
# Alignment-as-boundary-mathematics (Recognition #57) IS the
# structural property that keeps @magic/trick honest at the
# @cascade/code boundary. Misaligned @magic/trick = con/scam case.
# Aligned @magic/trick = honest-trick case. Same gauge surface;
# different matter mechanism; different boundary contract.
#
# === The gauge-theory reading ===
#
# Cross-language transpilation as gauge transformation:
#
# - `phone.rs` = local coordinate system (physical @io boundary)
# - @magic/trick = gauge transformation between representations of
#   the same underlying Eigenform
# - Rust ↔ mirror translation IS a gauge transformation — different
#   local descriptions of the same Eigenform-preserving content
# - @cascade/code/A/B species (@cascade/code/rust/llvm + @cascade/
#   code/llvm/turing + @cascade/code/turing/mirror per Mara #210) =
#   the gauge orbit between representations
# - Gauge-invariant = Eigenform-preserving properties: H¹ of light-
#   cone sheaf (Mara task #319 math root); Fiedler λ₀ = @coherence.
#   score (`shards/epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence.mirror`);
#   whole dH¹/dt ≤ 0 contraction per Mara task #314 Eigenform
#   Stabilizer synthesis at `ebd50a4`
#
# The Trick decidability requirement (Alex Wolf essay + Mara task
# #319 canonical spec): the honest trick requires sub-Turing substrate
# so @magic/trick can be VERIFIED at compile-time. Turing-complete
# substrate = @magic/trick may be Narcissus-aligned by construction
# (undecidable whether the trick is honest); sub-Turing substrate =
# @magic/trick can be Splinter-aligned by verification.
#
# === Substrate authority ===
#
# - **Family-root**: `shards/magic.mirror` (Recognition #80, 2026-06-19)
# - **Composition parents (substrate-decl via `in` imports)**:
#     @prism    — 5-op family per Recognition #79 basis
#     @meta     — substrate-decl marker at glass altitude
#     @glass    — imperfect / verdict / transparency carriers
#     @magic    — family-root; gauge-visible-with-matter-hidden
#                 discipline
#     @cascade  — A/B translation cascade family-root
#     @cascade/code — code-translation-specific cascade species
#     @bilateral — typed carrier for translation_admissible per
#                  Alex 2026-07-17 landing at `shards/epistemologic/
#                  pact/bilateral.mirror`
# - **Non-import cross-refs** (composition-graph, no `in`):
#     @void/splinter — aligned-trick pole (Splinter observer)
#     @void/narcissus — misaligned-trick pole (Narcissus observer)
#     @eigen — gauge-invariant = @eigen(T)-preserving
#     Recognition #57 — alignment-as-boundary-mathematics
# - **Canonical spec + math forward-promised**: docs/math + docs/specs
#   authoring by Mara territory next tick; this shard lands the
#   species-decl + bilaterals only
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word audit (clean) ===
#
# The word `trick` audit:
#
# - No prior `trick.mirror` shard exists at any altitude across
#   shards/ + spec/ + docs/ (grep clean 2026-07-22)
# - @magic docblock explicitly considered @trick as top-level
#   alternative and REJECTED it — verbatim: "@trick: deception
#   connotation; @magic carries both honest-trick and deception
#   variants via the Splinter/Narcissus pole choice." @magic/trick
#   as SPECIES inherits both poles at species altitude cleanly,
#   preserving the family-root's two-pole discipline.
# - Cultural resonance: stage magic IS a trick (audience sees
#   focus/project/split while mechanism is encapsulated behind
#   sleight); Alex Wolf's "The Trick" essay (systemic.engineering/
#   pieces/the-trick) names this at nervous-system altitude.
#
# Grep verdict CLEAN for this species altitude.
#
# === Composition surprises ===
#
# 1. **Same trick, different altitude.** @magic family-root's stage-
#    magic-as-encapsulation reading and @magic/trick's code-
#    translation-as-gauge-transformation reading are the SAME
#    substrate-mathematical shape at two altitudes. Recognition #80
#    established @magic as gauge-theory-operationalized; this species
#    is the compile-altitude realization at the @cascade/code
#    boundary. Not analogy — identity by structural specialisation.
#
# 2. **Aligned trick is the Kepler orbit of translation.** Per Mara
#    task #319 math root Chenciner-Montgomery extension: aligned
#    trick = translation whose two-body gauge orbit closes cleanly
#    (Kepler-like); misaligned trick = translation whose gauge orbit
#    is chaotic (three-body-problem-adjacent). Third-order stability
#    in translation is rare for the same reason third-order cognition
#    is rare: measure-zero set of the phase space.
#
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/magic/trick.mirror`
# declares `@magic/trick` and only that.

source @arxiv/cybernetics/foerster-2003
source @nl/systemic.engineering/pieces/the-trick

prism @magic/trick {
  focus  trick
  project trick
  split  trick
  shift  trick
  settle trick
}

# === the transform action — load-bearing ===
#
# transform(source, target_lang) -> imperfect(translated, ref, ref)
#
# The load-bearing gauge-transformation action. Given source content
# in language A and target language B, produce translated content in
# B whose Eigenform matches the source (Splinter pole) OR name the
# Eigenform-preservation failure explicitly (Narcissus pole).
#
# Returns imperfect per @glass discipline:
# - Success (aligned trick): translated content with Eigenform-
#   preservation verdict
# - Partial-with-loss: gauge-orbit approximation with named loss
#   per polyglot-loss-aware-computational-translation spec
#   (Mara task #207 landing)
# - Failure (misaligned trick): Eigenform-preservation cannot be
#   witnessed; substrate refuses the translation rather than
#   crystallizing dishonest content
#
# Body `\`-obligation-blocked per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]];
# consumers pull realization via `apply_h::act` bilateral resolver-
# arm dispatch (task #140 landing).
transform(source: ref, target_lang: ref) -> imperfect { \ }

# === the alignment-witness bilateral ===
#
# aligned_trick(source: ref, translated: ref) -> verdict
#
# Discharges Pass iff the translation preserves the source's
# Eigenform per @eigen(T) type-level equivalence. Composes over
# @bilateral(@code/rust, @code/mirror).translation_admissible +
# @coherence.score preservation across the gauge orbit + polyglot-
# loss-aware bounds.
bilateral aligned_trick {
  sentinel "magic-trick=aligned=eigenform-preserved-across-gauge-orbit"
  arity 2
}
aligned_trick(source: ref, translated: ref) -> verdict { \ }

# === the misalignment-detection bilateral ===
#
# misaligned_trick(source: ref, translated: ref) -> verdict
#
# Discharges Pass iff the translation violates Eigenform-preservation
# — the trick has drifted into Narcissus-pole territory (extractive,
# star-graph-collapse, contract-violation). Substrate-honest failure
# mode; consumers can enforce refusal on Pass verdict to prevent
# dishonest crystallization.
bilateral misaligned_trick {
  sentinel "magic-trick=misaligned=eigenform-violation-narcissus-pole"
  arity 2
}
misaligned_trick(source: ref, translated: ref) -> verdict { \ }

out @magic/trick
out transform
out aligned_trick
out misaligned_trick
